 ```
+
+### Temporal matte modes
+
+Temporal behavior can be selected at construction and changed without
+rebuilding the pipeline:
+
+```ts
+const pipeline = new EffectsPipeline(stream, {
+  background: 'blur',
+  temporalMode: 'stabilized', // 'stabilized' | 'warp-only' | 'off'
+})
+
+await pipeline.setTemporalMode('off')
+```
+
+`stabilized` preserves the flow-gated historical matte. `warp-only` uses
+optical flow only to fill skipped inference frames. `off` disables temporal
+history and runs current-frame segmentation on every source frame.
+
+### Protected startup
+
+Set `waitForFirstFrame: true` when publishing a background effect. This opt-in
+suppresses startup passthrough on every output transport and defers the video
+pipe until the model is attached. `ready` then waits for the first rendered
+output; bitmap-shuttle also waits for successful main-thread presentation.
+Initialization errors and destroy still reject readiness. The default remains
+passthrough during initialization for other SDK consumers.

 ## Performance presets

